## Architect validation (independent re-execution, not a re-read of this log)

Re-ran all 4 gates from scratch post-fix: tsc 0, vitest 77/12 0, i18n:check 0,
next build 0 (/settings 1.95 kB, unchanged). Cross-checked role-matrix.ts,
Sidebar.tsx, LocaleSwitcher.tsx, and the getTenantSettings resolver against
the claims above — all confirmed accurate. Base commit SHA verified via
`git rev-parse 02944fc`.

Two amendments applied (fix-in-passing, low severity, found during
validation — not present in Kiro's original delivery claims):

1. `page.tsx` — `useEffect` called `fetchSettings()` unconditionally before
   the `canSeeAdmin` guard ran, so Employee/Contractor roles issued a live
   `getTenantSettings` query even though the page renders `null` for them.
   Not a security issue (resolver has no role check; data isn't sensitive)
   but a wasted round-trip. Fixed: gate the effect on `canSeeSettings`.
2. `page.test.tsx` — the retry test drove the retry button with a raw DOM
   `.click()` instead of `fireEvent.click()`, causing React `act()` warnings
   (state updates outside act). Fixed: swapped to `fireEvent.click()`.

Both re-verified clean post-fix (act() warnings gone, all gates still green).

